From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:21:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 087/167] hjviewer: a PC that entered a support code marks its
 maker's login as staff
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W6, the PC's side (design w6-c6 3-5, 4-3, 4-4 "지원 확인", 5-4-4,
5-4-5; critic 2-2, 2-3): the answer that trades a support code for this
PC's ticket brings hjv-api's support grant ("staff"), signed with a list
key under "hjv-support-v1". The process that registers checks it as a
trust list is checked (src/hjviewer_account/grant.rs: a pinned list key,
the signature before the bytes, the ten members only, this PC's ID and
device key, a 32-byte account key, 1..=7200 s of life counted from
receipt), keeps it beside the ticket in memory only, and drops it with the
ticket: a new PC ticket replaces or clears it, hjv-guest-pc-end and the
process's end clear it. A grant refused leaves the ticket as it was.

While it holds a grant the PC sends Hash.hjv_nonce, also when it is not
installed. Right after a LoginRequest is latched, before every approval
branch, the connection sets self.hjv_staff when the request's
hjv-conn-v1 proof is by the grant's account key and fits this PC, this
nonce, the kind (remote, file, camera, terminal) and the grant's ctl_id.
try_start_cm then sends the controller's ID spaced as "123 456 789" in
place of the name the peer typed, with the mark {kind: "staff", who: ""}
(an accepted same-account proof still comes first). No new accept path:
self.authorized is never touched, upstream's click approval stays, and
input before [수락] is dropped as before. Design D11: a staff-marked login
without a password at a PC that takes clicks gets the unaccepted window
and No Password Access, also in 'both' mode with a valid password; at a
'password only' PC it goes on as any proof the PC does not take.

Test vectors for hjv-api's support-grant-vectors.json (design 6-1) were
computed with Python's cryptography from the byte layouts: the grant, the
proof (the v3 vectors' conn proof) and five refusals (another PC, bytes
changed after signing, 7201 s of life, an unknown member, another
account key's proof); support_json() renders the JSON copy.

hjv-e2e builds: the PC counts input dropped before authorization
(option hjv_e2e_dropped_input), the fake CM presses [수락] after
HJV_E2E_CM_ACCEPT_AFTER seconds, and --hjv-e2e-guest-pc-end ends this
PC's ticket and grant.

